# Auth API examples for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above any request. Requests are separated by ###.
#
# Run them top to bottom: later requests reuse the registered email and the login token.
# "Register" uses a new email each time ({{$timestamp}}), so you can re-run the file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@password = correct-horse-battery
@devPassword = Test1234!

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### HAPPY PATH
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Register (201, returns { token, user }, role is always EMPLOYEE)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "user{{$timestamp}}@shifthub.dev",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Register with "role": "MANAGER" (201, but role is still EMPLOYEE)
# The schema has no role field: Zod strips it, and the database default applies.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wannabe Manager",
  "email": "role{{$timestamp}}@shifthub.dev",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "role": "MANAGER"
}

### Login (200). Saves the token for the /me requests below.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{register.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current user (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### SHOULD FAIL
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### 409 EMAIL_TAKEN: same email as "Register" (different case: still taken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Copycat",
  "email": "{{register.request.body.$.email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 400 VALIDATION_ERROR: empty name, invalid email, short password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS: wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{register.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS: unknown email (same message as wrong password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 401 UNAUTHORIZED: /me without a token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### 401 UNAUTHORIZED: /me with a broken token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer this.is-not.a-valid-token

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### DEV USERS (run once per database, used by shifts.http)
### Blagoj is already registered (id 9). After registering, promote
### Blagoj to MANAGER in Prisma Studio, then run "Login Blagoj".
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Register Ana (201, EMPLOYEE). 409 if she already exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana",
  "email": "ana@shifthub.dev",
  "password": "{{devPassword}}"
}

### Register Marko (201, EMPLOYEE). 409 if he already exists.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Marko",
  "email": "marko@shifthub.dev",
  "password": "{{devPassword}}"
}

### Login Blagoj (200). After promotion: "role": "MANAGER"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "blagoj@shifthub.dev",
  "password": "{{devPassword}}"
}